    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From 0 to 10",
     "texto": [
      "- **nul** = 0\n- **en / et** = 1\n- **to** = 2\n- **tre** = 3\n- **fire** = 4\n- **fem** = 5\n- **seks** = 6\n- **syv** = 7\n- **otte** = 8\n- **ni** = 9\n- **ti** = 10"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«En» or «et»?",
     "texto": [
      "The number 1 has two forms, and which one you use depends on the **gender** of the word. English nouns have no gender like this, so it's new for you: **en kop** (a cup), **et glas** (a glass).\n\nWhen counting out loud, **en** is usually used: «en, to, tre…». We'll look at gender calmly in the café lesson."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A curiosity for later",
     "texto": [
      "From 0 to 10 everything is easy. But from 50 on, Danish numbers are formed in a very curious way, counting in twenties. We'll get there! For now, master these eleven."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
